    ],
    "formula": "<p>Pontos do nomograma (Granger 2003): <strong>idade</strong> &lt; 30 = 0, 30–39 = 8, 40–49 = 25, 50–59 = 41, 60–69 = 58, 70–79 = 75, 80–89 = 91, ≥ 90 = 100 · <strong>FC</strong> &lt; 50 = 0, 50–69 = 3, 70–89 = 9, 90–109 = 15, 110–149 = 24, 150–199 = 38, ≥ 200 = 46 · <strong>PAS</strong> &lt; 80 = 58, 80–99 = 53, 100–119 = 43, 120–139 = 34, 140–159 = 24, 160–199 = 10, ≥ 200 = 0 · <strong>creatinina</strong> (mg/dL) &lt; 0,4 = 1, 0,4–0,79 = 4, 0,8–1,19 = 7, 1,2–1,59 = 10, 1,6–1,99 = 13, 2–3,99 = 21, ≥ 4 = 28 · <strong>Killip</strong> I = 0, II = 20, III = 39, IV = 59 · parada cardíaca = 39 · desvio de ST = 28 · marcadores elevados = 14.</p><p>A probabilidade de óbito é lida no nomograma (interpolada entre os pontos tabelados).</p>",
    "sources": [
      [
        "Granger CB et al. Predictors of hospital mortality in the Global Registry of Acute Coronary Events. Arch Intern Med, 2003.",
        "https://doi.org/10.1001/archinte.163.19.2345"
      ],
      [
        "Byrne RA et al. 2023 ESC Guidelines for the management of acute coronary syndromes. Eur Heart J, 2023.",
        "https://doi.org/10.1093/eurheartj/ehad191"
      ]
    ],
